To update to a newer MXE version:

- Run the 'publish-mxe-toolchain' workflow manually from the Github Action
  GUI. Specify the ref (sha1 or branch) of the MXE version to be used (done
  in the UI when triggering the workflow). This workflow uses the
  .github/actions/setup-mxe-cairo action to complete the build.
  - Note that any changes to the workflow file need to be pushed to the
    default (i.e. for us, master) branch in order to take effect. 
    (FAOD: An ordinary rebuild with no changes can be done by just
    specifying the parameters above when triggering.)
- Make a note of the name of the resulting tarball and SHA-256 and update
  .github/actions/setup-mxe-cairo-download accordingly.
